From: Stephenuffugus <99242197+Stephenuffugus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:04:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] 3D: give the hiders a head start before the seekers can
 see anything
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stephen: "in a normal game the hider has a certain amount of time to hide before
the seeker is allowed to see anything until the time limit for the hider is up."

Rounds used to start with everyone loose at once, so a seeker could watch the
chameleons pick their spots — which is not hide and seek, it is just chase.

startRound now publishes hideEnds = now + HIDE_SECONDS (20), and the round clock
is extended by the same amount so the hunt itself is not shortened. While it runs:
  - the seeker is gated out of moveLocal and cannot beam (`active` is false)
  - detectAbductions returns early, so nobody can be caught
  - the seeker gets an opaque blindfold overlay with a countdown, because "not
    allowed to see anything" means the map must not be readable through it
  - hiders get their own banner: "Hide! N — the seekers are blind until this
    hits zero"

Verified with TWO real players in one Playroom room: the seeker came up
blindfolded with "The chameleons are choosing their spots", the hider saw "The
seekers are blind until this hits zero", and the blindfold lifted on its own when
the timer expired. 0 JS errors on either client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
